docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/R63.log:6:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018N7z3Nr3LZU525KU7f1wba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# R63 — Backend review — Phase 8 Workflow Engine V2\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** 8\n4\t**Type:** review\n5\t**Model class:** advanced\n6\t**Depends on:** T56, T57, T58, T59, T60, T61, T62\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2)\n8\t**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`); Definition of Done checklist (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Goal\n11\t\n12\tThis task delivers the Phase 8 backend review. It asserts that the redesigned workflow tools (T56, T57), the new memory tools (T58, T59, T60), the audited tool surface (T61), and the integrated outcome recorder + composition tests (T62) together satisfy spec §Phase 8 deliverables and definition of done, with no deferred scope and a tool surface that honors spec §MCP Surface \"Tool surface discipline.\" Without this review, Phase 9 metrics work proceeds against an unvalidated workflow surface and any spec gap discovered later requires reopening Phase 8.\n13\t\n14\t## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n15\t\n16\t> \"Phase 8 Deliverables: redesigned versions of context, change planning, scenario tracing, failure diagnosis, docs retrieval, test selection, impact analysis, and playbook generation; workflow composition over graph, event, memory, and working-memory substrates; one-call edit-planning bundles with code, docs, tests, memory, risks, and verification commands; workflow outcome recording integrated by default.\"\n17\t\n18\t> \"Definition of done: common coding tasks require fewer manual discovery calls; workflows produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping.\"\n19\t\n20\t> \"Tool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients … The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\" (spec §MCP Surface)\n21\t\n22\t## Inputs\n23\t\n24\t- Dependency outputs:\n25\t  - T56 — `workflow_v2/{prepare_change, plan_edit, trace_scenario, diagnose_failure}.rs` + edit-workflow tests.\n26\t  - T57 — `workflow_v2/{context_capsule, docs_capsule, relevant_tests, impact_from_diff}.rs` + discovery-workflow tests.\n27\t  - T58 — `memory_v2/{get_task_memory, save_memory, propose_memory_evolution}.rs` + memory-tool tests.\n28\t  - T59 — `memory_v2/{verify_explain_memory, list_memory_conflicts}.rs` + verify/explain tests.\n29\t  - T60 — `memory_v2/{consolidate_session, get_memory_metrics, get_event_trace}.rs` + admin-tool tests.\n30\t  - T61 — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` + `2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md`.\n31\t  - T62 — `workflow_v2/outcome_capture.rs` + composition tests.\n32\t- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n33\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (T02) for shim policy reconciliation.\n34\t  - The reviews directory `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/`.\n35\t- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Tests as documentation`, `## Observability`; Definition of Done checklist.\n36\t\n37\t## Steps\n38\t\n39\t1. Read spec §Phase 8 and §MCP Surface in full. Quote the definition-of-done paragraph verbatim at the top of the review.\n40\t2. Under `## Spec alignment`, walk every Phase 8 deliverable and cite the implementing files from T56–T62. Flag any deliverable that is missing, partial, or shimmed without a removal deadline.\n41\t3. Under `## Coding-standard alignment`, run a per-file check across `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/` and `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/`: file length ≤800 lines, function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10, schema parity (every public type derives serde), no `TODO`/`FIXME`/commented-out code, no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`, observability spans present. Record each violation with file:line.\n42\t4. Under `## Tool-surface size`, list the final shipped tool count (by name) and confirm it matches `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` exactly. Confirm every collapse decision from T61 is implemented in the actual code (e.g. `propose_memory_evolution(action=...)` and `verify_explain_memory(mode=...)` exist and the deprecation shims forward correctly). Flag any tool present in code but missing from the reference, or vice versa.\n43\t5. Under `## Findings`, summarize spec gaps, coding-standard violations, surface-size mismatches, hot-path budget regressions (T56 budget assertion, T62 recorder budget), shim policy gaps, and observability gaps. Each finding cites the file:line and the spec or standard it violates.\n44\t6. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::workflow_v2 rpc::memory_v2` and record the result in the review.\n45\t7. Under `## Verdict`, state `pass` or `fail` with a one-paragraph justification. If `fail`, name the specific tasks that must be reopened.\n46\t8. Save the review at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R63-workflow-engine-v2.md` with the mandatory headings checked by verification commands.\n47\t\n48\t## Files expected\n49\t\n50\t- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R63-workflow-engine-v2.md` — structured Phase 8 review with `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Tool-surface size`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict` headings; per-deliverable spec citations; per-file standard checks; build/test result; verdict with reopen list if `fail`.\n51\t\n52\t## Verification\n53\t\n54\t- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R63-workflow-engine-v2.md` — confirms the review exists at the harness path.\n55\t- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R63-workflow-engine-v2.md` — confirms spec alignment is recorded under a dedicated heading.\n56\t- `grep -q '## Tool-surface size' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R63-workflow-engine-v2.md` — confirms the surface-size check is recorded under a dedicated heading.\n57\t- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R63-workflow-engine-v2.md` — confirms a verdict is stated under a dedicated heading.\n58\t\n59\t## Coding-standard checks\n60\t\n61\t- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R63-workflow-engine-v2.md`).\n62\t- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — not applicable (review docs).\n63\t- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n64\t- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n65\t- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming — not applicable (review docs).\n66\t- For schema changes: review must flag any divergence between `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` and the implementations as a contract gate failure forwarded to R64.\n67\t- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2`, `## MCP Surface`, `## MCP Tool Contract Principles`; reference `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` and `2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md` from T61; reference `2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` from T02.\n68\t\n69\t## Definition of done\n70\t\n71\t- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n72\t- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n73\t- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n74\t- [ ] No deferred work: every Phase 8 spec deliverable is either implemented and cited, or recorded as a `fail` finding triggering reopen of the corresponding T-task.\n75\t- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the T02 compatibility policy was cross-referenced.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"589d9a30-530c-4e7c-8151-20cc70f1285a","uuid":"ab64058b-9265-4462-83ce-46b14c9ade96","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:38:50.092Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R63.md","content":"# R63 — Backend review — Phase 8 Workflow Engine V2\n\n**Phase:** 8\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T56, T57, T58, T59, T60, T61, T62\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`); Definition of Done checklist (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the Phase 8 backend review. It asserts that the redesigned workflow tools (T56, T57), the new memory tools (T58, T59, T60), the audited tool surface (T61), and the integrated outcome recorder + composition tests (T62) together satisfy spec §Phase 8 deliverables and definition of done, with no deferred scope and a tool surface that honors spec §MCP Surface \"Tool surface discipline.\" Without this review, Phase 9 metrics work proceeds against an unvalidated workflow surface and any spec gap discovered later requires reopening Phase 8.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 8 Deliverables: redesigned versions of context, change planning, scenario tracing, failure diagnosis, docs retrieval, test selection, impact analysis, and playbook generation; workflow composition over graph, event, memory, and working-memory substrates; one-call edit-planning bundles with code, docs, tests, memory, risks, and verification commands; workflow outcome recording integrated by default.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: common coding tasks require fewer manual discovery calls; workflows produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping.\"\n\n> \"Tool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients … The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\" (spec §MCP Surface)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T56 — `workflow_v2/{prepare_change, plan_edit, trace_scenario, diagnose_failure}.rs` + edit-workflow tests.\n  - T57 — `workflow_v2/{context_capsule, docs_capsule, relevant_tests, impact_from_diff}.rs` + discovery-workflow tests.\n  - T58 — `memory_v2/{get_task_memory, save_memory, propose_memory_evolution}.rs` + memory-tool tests.\n  - T59 — `memory_v2/{verify_explain_memory, list_memory_conflicts}.rs` + verify/explain tests.\n  - T60 — `memory_v2/{consolidate_session, get_memory_metrics, get_event_trace}.rs` + admin-tool tests.\n  - T61 — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` + `2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md`.\n  - T62 — `workflow_v2/outcome_capture.rs` + composition tests.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (T02) for shim policy reconciliation.\n  - The reviews directory `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/`.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Tests as documentation`, `## Observability`; Definition of Done checklist.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 8 and §MCP Surface in full. Quote the definition-of-done paragraph verbatim at the top of the review.\n2. Under `## Spec alignment`, walk every Phase 8 deliverable and cite the implementing files from T56–T62. Flag any deliverable that is missing, partial, or shimmed without a removal deadline.\n3. Under `## Coding-standard alignment`, run a per-file check across `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/` and `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/`: file length ≤800 lines, function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10, schema parity (every public type derives serde), no `TODO`/`FIXME`/commented-out code, no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`, observability spans present. Record each violation with file:line.\n4. Under `## Tool-surface size`, list the final shipped tool count (by name) and confirm it matches `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` exactly. Confirm every collapse decision from T61 is implemented in the actual code (e.g. `propose_memory_evolution(action=...)` and `verify_explain_memory(mode=...)` exist and the deprecation shims forward correctly). Flag any tool present in code but missing from the reference, or vice versa.\n5. Under `## Findings`, summarize spec gaps, coding-standard violations, surface-size mismatches, hot-path budget regressions (T56 budget assertion, T62 recorder budget), shim policy gaps, and observability gaps. Each finding cites the file:line and the spec or standard it violates.\n6. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::workflow_v2 rpc::memory_v2` and record the result in the review.\n7. Under `## Verdict`, state `pass` or `fail` with a one-paragraph justification. If `fail`, name the specific tasks that must be reopened.\n8. Save the review at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R63-workflow-engine-v2.md` with the mandatory headings checked by verification commands.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R63-workflow-engine-v2.md` — structured Phase 8 review with `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Tool-surface size`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict` headings; per-deliverable spec 