docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/R63.log:206:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015cEf19FUDbABkTcQryVUvm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six verification commands from tasks.json pass. The review is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nR63 is a Phase 8 backend review of the Workflow Engine V2 surface (T56–T62).\n\n**Verdict: fail.** The review documents:\n\n- **Spec alignment**: every Phase 8 deliverable cited to its implementing file in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/` and `memory_v2/`.\n- **Tool-surface size**: 49 advertised tools matching `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` exactly; the T61 collapse decisions (`propose_memory_evolution(action=…)` and `verify_explain_memory(mode=…)`) implemented with correctly-forwarding deprecation shims.\n- **Findings F-1..F-9**: four `rpc::memory_v2` tests fail under `cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib \"rpc::memory_v2\"` — `save_memory` rejects spec-conformant snake_case `memory_class` values; `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"propose\")` hits a FOREIGN KEY constraint on persistence; the apply-shim is blocked transitively; `get_task_memory` returns zero memories for a populated task scope. Additional Cadres `## Hard limits` violations recorded in F-5 (file/function/test lengths).\n- **Reopen list**: T58 primarily (F-1..F-4, F-6); T56/T57/T62 fold in F-5 refactors; T59/T60 re-run after fixes plus shrink `verify_explain_memory.rs` below the 800-line ceiling.\n\n`cargo build --release` passes; `rpc::workflow_v2` tests pass (18/18); `rpc::memory_v2` tests fail (13/17). Result written to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/results/R63.md`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":196,"cache_read_input_tokens":205705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":196},"output_tokens":1