y schema redesign: all required fields from spec §Memory Graph (stable id, content, class, assertion type, scope, verification status, confidence + reason, freshness policy, validity conditions, invalidation triggers, provenance events, evidence references, linked files/symbols/docs/tests/memories, contradiction/supersession links, access history, usefulness scores, last verified state). Classes include CounterMemory.\n- T20 — first-class link records (source, target, link type, strength, reason, evidence event, created_by, created_at, verification_status). Link types: supports/contradicts/supersedes/refines/generalizes/specializes/co_occurs_with/derived_from/applies_to/validated_by/invalidated_by.\n- T21 — streams from spec §ViLoMem (code topology, workflow episodes, failure patterns, semantic repo claims, architecture decisions, user/team preferences, docs and contract state). Scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization.\n- T22 — migration from existing `memories` table. Architecture doc required.\n- T23 — CRUD + verification status transitions (unverified → in_review → verified, plus stale/contradicted/superseded/expired/invalidated).\n- T24 — tests for contradiction, supersession, replay.\n- R18 reviews Phase 2 (event log) with P99 evidence; R25 reviews Phase 3 (memory graph) with CounterMemory coverage; R26 is the contract gate for Identity ↔ Event ↔ Memory.\n\nRead the spec yourself for the exact section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nWrite all 16 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed via ls. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code.","agentId":"ac92f5b374c3f7cf9","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 16 brief files written successfully.\n\n**File count: 16**\n\n**First 3 paths confirmed via ls:**\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R18.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R25.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R26.md`\n\n(Full set: T11–T17, R18, T19–T24, R25, R26.)\n\n**What was done:**\n- Read the spec (Phases 2/3, Storage Design, Memory Graph sections), the build context, the relevant tasks.json entries (lines 190–492 covering T11–R26), and the Cadres coding standard.\n- Wrote 14 task briefs and 2 review briefs at the requested paths, each following the exact template structures provided.\n- Each task file cites the matching spec heading via the anchor pattern, quotes 2–3 spec excerpts directly, lists files_expected and verification_commands verbatim from tasks.json, and gives 8–11 concrete steps tuned to the task type:\n  - T11: all 20 event kinds + envelope fields verbatim from spec §Event Log.\n  - T12: explicit column list for `events` and `event_payloads` with append-only triggers and indexes (task/session/workspace+branch/kind).\n  - T13: writer with payload hashing, spillover, workspace scoping, batched/sync flush; P99 budget called out (test sits in T17).\n  - T14: typed query builder with mandatory scope, ceilings, streaming, payload-corruption detection.\n  - T15: enumerates the workflow tools instrumented (`prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `get_context_capsule`, `expand_context`, `get_working_set_context`, `trace_scenario`, `summarize_subsystem`, `impact_from_diff`, `diagnose_failure`, `record_workflow_outcome`, `save_observation`) and the per-event helpers.\n  - T16: daemon-managed background compactor + versioned independently-readable snapshot header + `Bootstrap::load`; architecture doc required.\n  - T17: ordering/replay/corruption/scoping/P99 tests gated with `--include-ignored` for budget tests.\n  - T19: full 13-class taxonomy including CounterMemory + every spec-required field + denormalized scope columns + architecture doc.\n  - T20: all 11 link types, four first-class tables with explicit column lists, evidence anchors with span