s the exact template structure provided, with spec anchors using lowercase-dashed heading anchors, real cited spec excerpts, file-purpose lines for every `files_expected` path, per-command verification explanations, and the full definition-of-done checklist.\n- Review briefs (R05, R10) use the review template; R10 includes the mandatory `## P99 budget evidence` section because spec §Phase 1 DoD has the 2ms P99 SLA.\n- No code in `daemon/` or `extension/` was touched; tasks.json, context.md, and plan.md were not modified."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aede099a0ec974b60 (use SendMessage with to: 'aede099a0ec974b60' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 81442\ntool_uses: 20\nduration_ms: 367609</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"ae41cebd-19b0-442f-8ab2-5a3b65d21456","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:37:15.662Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are writing markdown task brief files for a build harness. Do NOT implement the feature itself — just write the brief markdown files at the exact paths I name.\n\nRepo root: /home/pete/cadres/lattice\nSpec: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md  (READ IT FIRST — Phases 0 and 1 sections)\nContext: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md\nTasks JSON: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks.json  (READ IT FIRST — extract title, depends_on, files_expected, verification_commands for each task you write)\nShared standards: /home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md  (read the \"Hard limits\" and \"No broken windows\" sections)\n\nWrite these 11 files, each at the path `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/<TASK_ID>.md`:\n\nT01, T02, T03, T04, R05, T06, T07, T08, T09, R10\n\n**Use this exact template structure (markdown) for each task file:**\n\n```\n# <TASK_ID> — <Title from tasks.json>\n\n**Phase:** <0 or 1>\n**Type:** <task_type from tasks.json>\n**Model class:** <model_class from tasks.json>\n**Depends on:** <depends_on list, comma-separated, or \"none\">\n**Spec anchor:** [§<Spec section name>](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#<lowercase-dashed-anchor>)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\n3–5 sentences. State what this task produces and why it matters for the substrate. Reference the spec's non-negotiables that apply.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> Direct quotes from the spec sections that bind this task (1-3 short quotes).\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: list the prior tasks' artifacts you read first.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on (cite exact paths under `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/` or `extension/src/`).\n- Standards files to honor: coding.md hard limits, AGENTS.md backward compatibility rules.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. ... concrete step\n2. ... concrete step\n3. ... etc. 5-10 steps each. Be specific about file edits, table schema, function signatures where the spec is explicit.\n\n## Files expected\n\nFor each path in tasks.json `files_expected`:\n- `path/to/file.ext` — one-line purpose.\n\n## Verification\n\nList each command from tasks.json `verification_commands` verbatim. Add a sentence under each explaining what passing means.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l <new files>`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming.\n- For schema changes: schema parity (every column has a corresponding field; nullability matches).\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Heading` from the spec or architecture doc that authorizes any non-obvious choice (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §<this phase> punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n```\n\n**For review files (R05, R10), use this template instead:**\n\n```\n# <REVIEW_ID> — <Title from tasks.json>\n\n**Phase:** Review for Phase <N>\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** <list>\n**Spec anchor:** [§<phase section>](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#<anchor>)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard, definition-of-done checklist.\n\n## Purpose\n\nWhat this review certifies. 2-3 sentences.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact produced by the listed dependency tasks.\n- Spec sections this phase claims to satisfy.\n- Shared standards: coding.md and definition-of-done-checklist.md sections relevant to this phase.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. ... step\n2. ... step\n... be specific about what to grep for, what tests to re-run, what schema columns to spot-check.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/<REVIEW_ID>-<slug>.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Spec alignment` — phase-by-phase coverage matrix.\n- `## Coding-standard alignment` — line-by-line audit vs. hard limits.\n- `## P99 budget evidence` (only for phases that have a P99 SLA in the spec).\n- `## Findings` — issues found, severity, suggested follow-up tasks (do NOT defer outside this build).\n- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n\n## Verification\n\nList each command from tasks.json verbatim with a sentence explaining what passing means.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content.\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session).\n```\n\n**Task-specific content guidance:**\n\n- T01 produces `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-fork-or-extend-decision.md`. The decision considers the four gate conditions in spec §Phase 0 (breaking memories table changes, identity primary-key changes, event log requiring incompatible WAL changes, two-or-more of the above). The decision MUST document evidence and a branch-or-repo name.\n- T02 produces architecture overview (workspace graph, event log, memory graph sections required) + MCP compatibility policy (backward compatibility required).\n- T03 names new crates `lattice-identity`, `lattice-events`, `lattice-memory`, `lattice-retrieval`, `lattice-working-memory`, `lattice-consolidation`, `lattice-verification` (live under daemon/crates/) OR documents why they're modules in `lattice-core` instead. Storage migration policy must include migration order and rollback.\n- T04 captures baseline benchmarks of EXISTING workflows so Phase 4/9 has something to regress against. Bench file uses criterion conventions.\n- T06–T09 implement the unified identity model from spec §Phase 1: stable IDs for files, symbols, docs, sections, events, memories, context handles; identity resolver with ambiguity diagnostics; serialization in MCP payloads; legacy name compat. P99 budget ≤2ms.\n- R05 reviews Phase 0; R10 reviews Phase 1 (must include \"P99 budget evidence\" section).\n\nRead the spec yourself for the exact spec section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nWrite all 11 files. Then report a one-line confirmation per file with `ls -la` style output. Do NOT modify tasks.json. Do NOT modify context.md or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code in daemon/ or extension/.","agentId":"aede099a0ec974b60","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 11 requested files exist (T01, T02, T03, T04, R05, T06, T07, T08, T09, R10). Note: the directory also contained additional unrelated task briefs (T11-T72) that appear to have been created in a parallel session — I did not touch those.\n\nConfirmation of the 11 files written by this task:\n\n- `-rw-rw-r-- T01.md` (6,409 bytes) — Phase 0 fork-or-extend decision doc\n- `-rw-rw-r-- T02.md` (6,909 bytes) — Phase 0 architecture overview + MCP compatibility policy\n- `-rw-rw-r-- T03.md` (7,008 bytes) — Phase 0 crate boundary plan + storage migration policy\n- `-rw-rw-r-- T04.md` (6,816 bytes) — Phase 0 baseline benchmark capture\n- `-rw-rw-r-- R05.md` (6,150 bytes) — Foundation review for Phase 0\n- `-rw-rw-r-- T06.md` (7,543 bytes) — Phase 1 identity type system\n- `-rw-rw-r-- T07.md` (6,810 bytes) — Phase 1 identity resolver with ambiguity diagnostics\n- `-rw-rw-r-- T08.md` (6,685 bytes) — Phase 1 identity serialization in MCP + legacy shim\n- `-rw-rw-r-- T09.md` (6,931 bytes) — Phase 1 identity test matrix + P99 budget tests\n- `-rw-rw-r-- R10.md` (6,567 bytes) — Backend review for Phase 1 identity substrate (includes mandatory `## P99 budget evidence` section)\n\nSummary of what was done:\n- Read spec §Phase 0 and §Phase 1 in full and quoted bound passages verbatim in each brief.\n- Read tasks.json entries for T01-T09, R05, R10 and used the exact `title`, `depends_on`, `files_expected`, and `verification_commands` from each entry.\n- Read coding.md hard-limits and no-broken-windows sections and propagated those checks into each brief's `## Coding-standard checks` block.\n- Each task brief follows the exact template structure provided, with spec anchors using lowercase-dashed heading anchors, real cited spec excerpts, file-purpose lines for every `files_expected` path, per-command verification explanations, and the full definition-of-done checklist.\n- Review briefs (R05, R10) use the review template; R10 includes the mandatory `## P99 budget evidence` section because spec §Phase 1 DoD has the 2ms P99 SLA.\n- No code in `daemon/` or `extension/` was touched; tasks.json, context.md, and plan.md were not modified."}],"totalDurationMs":367609,"totalTokens":81442,"totalToolUseCount":20,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":79289,"output_tokens":934,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1218},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":934,"cache_read_input_tokens":79289,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1218,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":5,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":3,"editFileCount":10,"linesAdded":749,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T37.log:2072:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2728:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:725:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VT8gipuad96TX8SiC5vJU9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JvZswMJm52WEk12Gy4ztFp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T32.md","content":"# T32 — Phase 4 — Retrieval benchmark suite + golden anchors + ranking tests\n\n**Phase:** 4\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T27, T28, T29, T30, T31\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 4: Retrieval V1](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-4-retrieval-v1), [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task closes Phase 4 with the benchmark suite, golden anchor fixtures, and ranking regression tests required by spec §Phase 4 deliverables (\"benchmark suite for realistic assistant tasks\") and §Phase 4 Definition of Done (\"irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed\"). The benchmark must measure end-to-end retrieval against a fixed set of representative tasks, the golden anchor tests must pin the anchor-resolution behaviour against a curated corpus, and ranking regression tests must guard against silent reordering of the ranked output as future signals are tuned. Metrics are written to a baseline JSON file under `docs/plans/.../baselines/` so future runs can diff against it without re-reading the test fixtures.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 4: Retrieval V1 — Deliverables: ... benchmark suite for realistic assistant tasks.\" (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)\n\n> \"Definition of done: ... irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed.\" (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)\n\n> \"Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation — Deliverables: golden benchmark task set; precision/recall measurement for retrieved memory; usefulness measurement; freshness and staleness metrics; consolidation throughput metrics; CLI for metrics reporting.\" (spec §Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T27 intent classifier, T28 anchor resolver, T29 candidate retrieval, T30 scorer + diagnostics, T31 shaper — the full Phase 4 pipeline is in place before this task runs.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/benchmark_tests.rs` and `query/benchmark_tests.rs` — convention for benchmark-style tests under `cargo test -- --include-ignored`.\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/` (created earlier in the build) — directory the baseline metrics JSON is written into.\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (tests as documentation: one test per behaviour, ≤30 lines per test, named for the behaviour); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (verification is real shell commands).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Re-read spec §Phase 4 deliverables and Definition of Done, and §Phase 9 metrics list, to fix the metrics the benchmark must emit: top-K precision, top-K recall, irrelevant-memory rate, mean rank of golden result, P50/P95 retrieval latency, candidates per source, dedupe rate, truncation rate.\n2. Curate a golden anchor corpus in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/golden_tests.rs` covering each anchor type (path, symbol, error string, command, API name, config key) with at least three task statements per type, the expected resolved identities, and the expected top-1 result identity. The corpus is in code (not external fixtures) so the test is hermetic.\n3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/benchmark.rs` as an `#[ignore]`d test that builds a synthetic workspace (small fixture graph + memories + events), runs the full retrieval pipeline against the golden corpus, computes the metrics list above, asserts against pinned thresholds documented inline, and writes the metric snapshot to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/retrieval_v1_metrics.json`. The `#[ignore]` lets `cargo test` stay fast while CI runs `cargo test -- --include-ignored`.\n4. Implement ranking regression tests in `golden_tests.rs`: for every golden task, assert that the top-1 result is the expected identity, that the second result is not a stale memory unless the task expects one, and that the inclusion reason for the top result mentions the dominant signal (e.g. an exact-symbol-match task surfaces \"exact identifier match\" in the reason). Tests are ≤30 lines each.\n5. Pin a stale-memory regression: include at least one golden task where a stale memory exists in the fixture and assert that the stale memory ranks below the trusted result, per spec §Stale Memory Leakage control.\n6. Pin a budget regression: include at least one golden task with a deliberately-oversized candidate set and assert that truncation flips `BudgetReport::truncated`, that pinned results survive truncation, and that the bundle still ships within the documented token cap.\n7. Write `retrieval_v1_metrics.json` schema documentation as a doc comment at the top of `benchmark.rs`: every field, its meaning, its threshold, and the rule for tightening it.\n8. Add a CLI hook (small Rust binary entry under the existing benchmark scaffolding, or a `cargo run --example retrieval_v1_metrics`) only if the existing benchmark convention supports it; otherwise the `--include-ignored` test alone satisfies the verification command. Document the convention chosen at the top of `benchmark.rs`.\n9. Run all four verification commands locally; fix any clippy warnings before stopping.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/benchmark.rs` — benchmark harness, metric computation, baseline-JSON writer.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/golden_tests.rs` — golden anchor corpus and ranking regression tests.\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/retrieval_v1_metrics.json` — pinned baseline metrics emitted by the benchmark.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/benchmark.rs` — confirms the benchmark module exists at the expected path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/golden_tests.rs` — confirms the golden-test module exists at the expected path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::golden_tests` — runs the golden-anchor and ranking-regression tests.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::benchmark -- --include-ignored` — runs the benchmark and emits the baseline metrics JSON.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file. If the golden corpus grows beyond the cap, split into `golden_tests/` submodules grouped by anchor kind.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Each test ≤30 lines per `coding.md` \"Tests as documentation\".\n- Schema parity: `retrieval_v1_metrics.json` field set mirrors the `BenchmarkMetrics` struct in `benchmark.rs` exactly; both are updated in the same commit.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Single source of truth: thresholds live in `benchmark.rs` as documented constants; they are not duplicated in `golden_tests.rs`.\n- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every test is named for the behaviour it asserts (e.g. `test_exact_symbol_anchor_returns_correct_identity`).\n- Doc citation: thresholds cite `## Phase 4: Retrieval V1` (Definition of Done) and `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every metric the spec names (top-K precision/recall, irrelevant-memory rate, latency) is computed by the benchmark; every anchor type has at least one golden test; the stale-memory and truncation regressions are pinned.\n- [ ] `retrieval_v1_metrics.json` is checked in with realistic baseline values produced by an actual benchmark run, not placeholders.\n- [ ] The Phase 4 Definition-of-Done item \"irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed\" has a single named test that asserts it.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3760,"cache_read_input_tokens":59914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3760,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019RjXwCuf57BAKn88mWkE24","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"c811ffb9-e710-45cb-baa8-2368ee072044","request_id":"req_011Cb7N3i9H91jNL98UqmPGP","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 4+5 task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T37.log:2073:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2729:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:728:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DKqsA9GSR28Z9docHMsRqr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EUFHk1ywsQwkYwKK5eG5uN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md","content":"# T60 — Phase 8 — New tools: consolidate_session + get_memory_metrics + get_event_trace\n\n**Phase:** 8\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** R55\n**Spec anchor:** [§MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task introduces the three remaining new MCP tools from spec §MCP Surface: `consolidate_session` (trigger session-level consolidation producing episode/procedure/failure-pattern proposals), `get_memory_metrics` (return the assistant-usefulness signals required by spec §Phase 9), and `get_event_trace` (return a paginated event-log slice scoped by task/session/workspace for audit and replay). Together these three tools complete the new memory surface and make the underlying substrates inspectable from any MCP client. Without them, Phase 6 consolidation runs only autonomously, Phase 9 metrics surface nothing to assistants, and the Phase 2 event log is invisible — all violations of spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties \"every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable\" and §MCP Tool Contract Principles.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"New or redesigned memory tools: …`consolidate_session`, `get_memory_metrics`, `get_event_trace`.\" (spec §MCP Surface)\n\n> \"Consolidation modes: synchronous post-task consolidation for small task traces; background scheduled consolidation for larger histories; manual review mode for high-impact repo or organization memories; replay mode for rebuilding memory state from the event log.\" (spec §Consolidation Engine)\n\n> \"Required metrics: tool calls per successful task; irrelevant files opened per task; relevant anchor recall; memory inclusion precision; memory later-used rate; stale memory surfaced rate; contradiction missed rate; tests recommended versus tests needed; workflow success after first plan.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n> \"The fucore/src/verification/expiry.rs\",\n        \"test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/incremental.rs\",\n        \"cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification::incremental_tests\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T52\",\n      \"title\": \"Phase 7 — Stale surfacing in workflow bundles + label discipline (no trusted display of stale/contradicted)\",\n      \"task_type\": \"backend\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T48\", \"T49\", \"T50\", \"T51\"],\n      \"model_class\": \"advanced\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"files_expected\": [\n        \"daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/surfacing.rs\",\n        \"daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/surfacing_tests.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"verification_commands\": [\n        \"test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/surfacing.rs\",\n        \"cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification::surfacing_tests\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"T53\",\n      \"title\": \"Phase 7 — Verification tests (stale never displayed as trusted, scope leakage blocked)\",\n      \"task_type\": \"tests\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T48\", \"T49\", \"T50\", \"T51\", \"T52\"],\n      \"model_class\": \"balanced\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"files_expected\": [\n        \"daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/integration_tests.rs\"\n     