docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:5601:This task delivers the memory inbox — the operator's primary list view over every memory the daemon knows about. It mounts inside the review panel scaffolding from T71, lists memories with filterable columns (status, scope, class), and renders one status badge per row covering all eight verification states from spec §Verification Engine. The inbox is the entry point operators use to find the memory they want to verify, accept, reject, or inspect — without it, the promotion queue (T73), contradiction queue (T73), stale view (T74), and evidence inspector (T74) have nothing to link to. Spec §10 lists "memory inbox" first among the required operator views, which fixes its position as the spine of the review surface.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:5629:8. Wire the row click handler to post a message back to `ReviewPanelProvider` requesting navigation to the evidence inspector (T74). Wire the "Open Trace" action to request navigation to the event trace view (T75).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:5658:- All modals via native `<dialog>` — the inbox itself does not open modals (action buttons route to T73/T74 which own their dialogs), but any inline confirm (e.g. "Clear all filters?") uses `<dialog>` or routes through `vscode.window.showInformationMessage` with explicit actions. Never `window.confirm/prompt/alert`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:5670:- [ ] No deferred work: all filter axes from spec §10 wired in this task; row-click navigation handed off to T74/T75 (sibling tasks), not deferred.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:5717:7. Cross-link: clicking a failed consolidation job opens the event trace view (T75) filtered to the related task/session; clicking a broken-reference row opens the file or symbol via `vscode.commands.executeCommand('vscode.open', uri)`; clicking a stale-edge row opens the evidence inspector (T74) for the related memory if one exists.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:5759:- [ ] UI specification checks satisfied: queue-depth indicator with bound + dropped-job warning per spec §6; per-family counts for all spec §2 node/edge families; cross-navigation to T74/T75 wired through router.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:5845:- [ ] No deferred work: both queues + the shared dialog ship in this task; stale view (T74), event trace (T75), and graph/index health (T76) are sibling tasks, not deferrals.
