or extractor for all 6 spec-named types (paths/symbols/errors/commands/APIs/config keys) routing through Phase 1 IdentityResolver; hybrid candidate retrieval covering all 9 spec-named sources with budget enforcement; scorer implementing every one of the 13 spec-named ranking signals with diagnostic mode; compact shaper with non-optional `inclusion_reason` and `expansion_handle` plus Phase 5 forward-compatibility contract; benchmark + golden anchors + ranking regression tests writing baseline JSON; review with required headings `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Inclusion-reason discipline`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- **Phase 5 (T34–T37, R38):** `WorkingMemoryState` carrying all 11 spec-named fields plus typed `ExcludedMemory.exclusion_reason`; `working_memory_checkpoints` table with versioned schema and SHA-256 hash; all 8 spec-named operations (retrieve/summarize/filter/pin/evict/expand/compress/checkpoint) with idempotency and pin-protection contracts; MCP `inspect_working_memory` tool plus automatic event capture wiring `MemoryRetrieved`/`MemoryExpanded` events from Phase 2; 4 test families (budgets/pins/eviction/checkpoint restore); review with required headings `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Excluded-context auditability`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n\nEvery brief uses the T01 template (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks, Definition of done), quotes the exact spec headings verbatim, lists 7–10 concrete steps, names the exact file paths from `tasks.json` `files_expected`, copies the exact `verification_commands` from `tasks.json`, and includes the requested coding-standard items (file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, schema parity for the SQL task T34, no broken windows). No tasks.json, context.md, plan.md, or implementation code was modified."}],"totalDurationMs":647944,"totalTokens":90189,"totalToolUseCount":30,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cach