/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md\n\nWrite these 12 files at `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/<TASK_ID>.md`:\n\nT27, T28, T29, T30, T31, T32, R33, T34, T35, T36, T37, R38\n\n**Use the same template structure as the prior agents** (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks, Definition of done) for work tasks; for review tasks use the review template with required headings.\n\n**Task-specific guidance:**\n\n- T27 — intent classifier: classify user task by type (debug/refactor/explain/add-feature/test/docs/migration/etc.). Should be feature-based and inspectable per spec §Ranking Complexity risk.\n- T28 — anchor extractor: extract paths, symbols, errors, commands, APIs, config keys; resolve into graph identities using identity resolver from Phase 1.\n- T29 — hybrid candidate retrieval: exact path/symbol lookup + code graph traversal + doc backlinks/outgoing links + FTS + embeddings + event similarity + memory links + workflow similarity + recent working memory.\n- T30 — scoring with ALL signals from spec §Retrieval Engine \"Ranking signals\": task-type compatibility, graph proximity, exact identifier match, semantic similarity, verification status, freshness, scope, evidence strength, contradiction/supersession state, past usefulness, recent successful reuse, user preference compatibility, token cost. Diagnostic mode exposes scores AND reasons.\n- T31 — compact response shaper: every result has an `inclusion_reason` and an `expansion_handle`. Forward-compatible with Phase 5 working memory checkpoints per spec §Phase 4 scope constraint.\n- T32 — benchmark suite + golden anchors + ranking regression tests.\n- R33 — Phase 4 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Inclusion-reason discipline`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- T34 — working memory state from spec §Working Memory: task statement, interpreted intent, active files/symbols, active hypotheses, active failures, current plan, selected memories, excluded memories and reasons, budget decisions, unresolved questions, verification status. Table: `working_memory_checkpoints`.\n- T35 — operations: retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, checkpoint.\n- T36 — MCP tool for inspection + event capture for include/exclude reasons (`MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded` events from Phase 2).\n- T37 — tests: budgets, pinned context, eviction, checkpoint restore.\n- R38 — Phase 5 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Excluded-context auditability`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nFor each task, include 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths (from tasks.json `files_expected`), and the exact verification commands from tasks.json. The \"Coding-standard checks\" section should include: file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, schema parity for SQL tasks, no broken windows.\n\nWrite all 12 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code.","agentId":"a8b9cf908dfeed8f7","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 12 task brief files written successfully.\n\n**Files written: 12**\n\n**First 3 paths confirmed:**\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T27.md` (intent classifier)\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T28.md` (anchor extractor + resolver)\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md` (hybrid candidate retrieval)\n\n**All 12 files:** T27, T28, T29, T30, T31, T32, R33, T34, T35, T36, T37, R38.\n\n**Coverage summary:**\n- **Phase 4 (T27–T32, R33):** Intent classifier with feature-based ranker per §Ranking Complexity; anchor extractor for all 6 spec-named types (paths/symbols/errors/commands/APIs/config keys) routing through Phase 1 IdentityResolver; hybrid candidate retrieval covering all 9 spec-named sources with budget enforcement; scorer implementing every one of the 13 spec-named ranking signals with diagnostic mode; compact shaper with non-optional `inclusion_reason` and `expansion_handle` plus Phase 5 forward-compatibility contract; benchmark + golden anchors + ranking regression tests writing baseline JSON; review with required headings `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Inclusion-reason discipline`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- **Phase 5 (T34–T37, R38):** `WorkingMemoryState` carrying all 11 spec-named fields plus typed `ExcludedMemory.exclusion_reason`; `working_memory_checkpoints` table with versioned schema and SHA-256 hash; all 8 spec-named operations (retrieve/summarize/filter/pin/evict/expand/compress/checkpoint) with idempotency and pin-protection contracts; MCP `inspect_working_memory` tool plus automatic event capture wiring `MemoryRetrieved`/`MemoryExpanded` events from Phase 2; 4 test families (budgets/pins/eviction/checkpoint restore); review with required headings `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Excluded-context auditability`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n\nEvery brief uses the T01 template (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks, Definition of done), quotes the exact spec headings verbatim, lists 7–10 concrete steps, names the exact file paths from `tasks.json` `files_expected`, copies the exact `verification_commands` from `tasks.json`, and includes the requested coding-standard items (file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, schema parity for the SQL task T34, no broken windows). No tasks.json, context.md, plan.md, or implementation code was modified."}],"totalDurationMs":647944,"totalTokens":90189,"totalToolUseCount":30,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":88692,"output_tokens":1080,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":416},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1080,"cache_read_input_tokens":88692,"cache_creation_input_tokens":416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":416,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":9,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":7,"editFileCount":12,"linesAdded":938,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:8014:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T41.log:1978:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2746:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:841:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0158fayGk8TdCJvKN5fwBobH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QuEbpAPeDTAh2At2PyM8AZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T67.md","content":"# T67 — Phase 9 — get_memory_metrics + retrieval relevance surfaces wired through MCP\n\n**Phase:** 9\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T65\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task wires the T65 metrics module through the MCP surface so the `get_memory_metrics` tool from T60 returns the full canonical signal set rather than the fallback session_metrics view, and adds per-call retrieval relevance surfaces (inclusion reasons, scoring breakdowns) into the existing workflow tool responses. Spec §Phase 9 Deliverables names \"retrieval relevance metrics\" as binding, and spec §Phase 4 Definition of Done requires \"workflow tools return memory with inclusion reasons and stable expansion handles … irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed.\" Without this task, the metrics module ships but no MCP client can read it and no per-call relevance signal is exposed.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 9 Deliverables: retrieval relevance metrics; memory usefulness metrics; context token efficiency metrics; stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics.\"\n\n> \"Workflow tools return memory with inclusion reasons and stable expansion handles … irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed.\" (spec §Phase 4 DoD)\n\n> \"The ranker should expose scores and reasons in diagnostic mode. Compact mode should include only enough explanation for an assistant to trust the result.\" (spec §Retrieval Engine)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T65 — `MetricsCollector`, `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricScope`.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs` (T60) — current implementation reading from fallback session_metrics; T67 swaps it to consume `MetricsCollector` directly.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/` (T56/T57) — each tool's response carries `MemoryHighlight`s; T67 extends them with per-call relevance scoring.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — MCP tool registration.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs` — for handle-driven expansion of relevance details.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Observability`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 9, §Retrieval Engine, and §Phase 4 DoD in full.\n2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs` as the MCP-facing facade over the T65 `MetricsCollector`. It exposes: (a) `MetricsSurface::collect(scope, signals)` calling the T65 collector and returning `Vec<MetricValue>`; (b) `MetricsSurface::collect_for_call(task_id, tool_name)` returning per-call relevance: per-pivot inclusion score breakdown (graph proximity, semantic similarity, freshness, scope, verification, evidence strength, past usefulness — per spec §Retrieval Engine \"Ranking signals\"), per-memory inclusion reason, excluded high-scoring candidates with rejection reasons; (c) `MetricsSurface::summarize_for_compact_mode(...)` returning a one-line digest suitable for compact tool responses.\n3. Wire `metrics_surface.rs` into `memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs` so the tool reads from the T65 collector through this facade rather than the fallback `session_metrics`. The fallback path remains as an explicit `source: SessionMetrics` value when the collector returns `None` for a given signal — never fabricate a value.\n4. Extend the T56/T57 workflow tools' responses to attach per-call relevance via `MetricsSurface::collect_for_call`. In `compact` render mode each `MemoryHighlight` and `Pivot` carries the summarized one-line digest; in `full` / `diagnostic` mode each carries the full score breakdown. Spec §Retrieval Engine: \"The ranker should expose scores and reasons in diagnostic mode.\"\n5. Add a stable expansion handle (`relevance_detail_handle`) on every `MemoryHighlight` and `Pivot` so `expand_context` can fetch the full diagnostic breakdown without re-running the workflow.\n6. Workspace boundary + scope-leak protections: every `MetricsSurface::collect_for_call` query honors workspace and scope filters, matching the discipline established in T58–T60.\n7. In `metrics_surface_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) round-trip the surface's request/response through serde; (b) assert the surface returns every T65 `MetricSignal` variant; (c) assert it returns `null` with a reason when no data is available, never a fabricated value; (d) assert per-call relevance includes every ranking-signal column from spec §Retrieval Engine; (e) assert compact mode digests are bounded in size; (f) assert the diagnostic expansion handle dereferences to the full breakdown; (g) assert workspace boundary and scope filters reject cross-scope queries with a typed error.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs` — MCP-facing facade exposing `collect`, `collect_for_call`, `summarize_for_compact_mode`; wires T65 `MetricsCollector` into `get_memory_metrics` (T60) and extends T56/T57 workflow responses with per-call relevance breakdowns and stable expansion handles per spec §Retrieval Engine.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface_tests.rs` — unit tests covering serde round-trip, full signal-set coverage, honest null reporting, per-call relevance breakdown, compact-mode digest bound, expansion-handle dereference, scope-leak rejection.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/metrics_surface.rs` — confirms the surface file exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::metrics_surface_tests` — every metrics-surface test passes (serde round-trip, signal coverage, honest null, per-call breakdown, compact digest bound, expansion-handle dereference, scope-leak rejection).\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: `MetricsSurface` request/response types reuse `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricSource`, `MetricScope` from T65; do not introduce parallel types; every public field has a doc comment.\n- No silent error handling — missing data is honest `None` with reason; scope-leak rejections are typed errors.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`MetricsSurface::collect_for_call`, not `MetricsSurface::call_metrics`).\n- For SQLite: storage access flows through T65 collector; no raw SQL in the RPC surface.\n- Observability: surface emits `tracing::info!` spans with `tool`, `scope`, `signal_count`, `source_breakdown` fields.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation`, `## Retrieval Engine`, `## Phase 4 — Retrieval V1` DoD in module doc comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every T65 signal is reachable via `get_memory_metrics`; every T56/T57 workflow response carries per-call relevance + expansion handle in this task — not \"to be added later.\"\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; the legacy `session_metrics` view continues to respond per the T02 compatibility policy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3897,"cache_read_input_tokens":99814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3897,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"a198de81-caba-4d7a-a742-bf4416702711","request_id":"req_011Cb7NUqgQADaeKzWbKLxf2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
