docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:7:> Tool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md:16:| Collapse `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` into canonical `verify_explain_memory` with `mode` values `verify`, `explain`, and `verify_and_explain`. | Verification and explanation share the same evidence checks, status taxonomy, confidence delta, and expansion handle. Keeping two canonical tools would duplicate result semantics and make clients choose between freshness and diagnostics. | [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) explicitly asks whether `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` can be unified. [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles) requires memory-bearing responses to identify evidence strength, verification status, freshness, and explanation metadata. | `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` remain advertised deprecated shims in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs`; each forces the appropriate `mode` and attaches `deprecation_warning`. | Remove no earlier than one full numbered phase cycle after Phase 8 once maintained clients have migrated to `verify_explain_memory`, following [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). |
